On Wed, 14 Oct 2026 03:03:41 -0700, Pat Maddox <pat@patmaddox.com> wrote:
> Add a `just process-email` just task that does the work
> deterministically. It should:

It is posted as "[PATCH v2 0/7] Add just process-email" [1]. Most of
it was already on the list, unreviewed, in "[PATCH 0/3] Add just
process-email" [2] and "[PATCH 0/2] Get up to date deterministically
before process-email" [3]. v2 folds both into one series against
trunk and adds the notification. The loop takes no control signal
from claude's output, which goes to /dev/null; it reads the inbox
from notmuch.

> 1. update the jj mail dir
> 2. notmuch index

Each pass starts with `just get-up-to-date`. It fetches every remote,
rebases my trunk work and my mail outbox onto upstream, starts a fresh
change in the mail workspace, and runs notmuch new.

> 3. check for inbox messages. if there are any, process them one at a time,
> oldest first. for each one, notify ${NOTIFY_URL}

It takes the oldest inbox message and runs a fresh
`claude --permission-mode auto -p "/process-email <id>"` on it. Then
it checks with notmuch that the message left the inbox. The loop, not
the model, posts "answered: <subject>" to the topic, since only the
loop knows from the inbox whether the pass worked. A post that fails
or takes over ten seconds only warns.

> 4. when there are no inbox messages, exit

It exits 0 when the inbox is empty. There is one more exit: if a pass
leaves its message in the inbox, it notifies "stuck: <subject>" and
exits 1. Without that, it would run claude on the same message
forever. Tell me if you would rather it skip the message and go on.

> NOTIFY_URL will be provided as a secret, similar to how we provide mail
> secrets for lab-mail jail.

lab-claude now mounts /jails/data/lab-claude/secrets read-only at
/data/secrets, the way lab-mail does, and the loop reads the URL from
notify-url there. NOTIFY_URL in the environment overrides the file.
With neither set, it posts nothing. To set it up on beastie, then
restart lab-claude:

    mkdir -p /jails/data/lab-claude/secrets
    cd /jails/data/lab-claude/secrets
    printf '%s\n' 'https://ntfy.sh/<topic>' > notify-url
    chown -R 0:15000 .
    chmod 0750 .
    chmod 0640 notify-url

The series also declares ftp/curl in lab-claude's packages. curl is
already installed in the jail, but only as another package's
dependency.

Then the loop you run today becomes:

    just process-email

